Input: {"question": "When was Porush born?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0364-395b1e3fa824:d00", "start": 0, "end": 237, "text": "Meir Porush Meir Porush (, born 11 June 1955) is an Israeli politician who has served as a member of the Knesset for the ultra-Orthodox Agudat Yisrael faction of United Torah Judaism between 1996 and 2011, and again from 2013 until 2016."}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0364-395b1e3fa824:d00", "start": 238, "end": 287, "text": "He is currently the Deputy Minister of Education."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0364-395b1e3fa824:d00", "start": 288, "end": 322, "text": "Meir Porush was born in Jerusalem."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0364-395b1e3fa824:d00", "start": 323, "end": 415, "text": "His father Rabbi Menachem Porush (1916–2010) was one of the longest-serving Knesset members."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0364-395b1e3fa824:d00", "start": 416, "end": 447, "text": "Meir was educated in a yeshiva."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0364-395b1e3fa824:d00", "start": 448, "end": 559, "text": "After leaving yeshiva, Porush served in the IDF, and supports further Haredi participation in military service."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0364-395b1e3fa824:d00", "start": 560, "end": 610, "text": "Porush lives in Jerusalem with his wife and twelve"}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0364-395b1e3fa824:d01", "start": 0, "end": 632, "text": "1,063 ; 183 KB 0 references sex or gender male 1 reference based on heuristic inferred from person's given name country of citizenship Israel 0 references name in native language מאיר פרוש (Hebrew) 1 reference imported from Wikimedia project Russian Wikipedia Wikimedia import URL https://ru.wikipedia.org/?oldid=121636666 given name Meir 1 reference based on heuristic inferred from person's full name family name Porush 0 re