4:d03", "start": 223, "end": 365, "text": "Porush, a seventh-generation Jerusalemite, was born in Jerusalem in 1916 to Rabbi Moshe Glickman-Porush, and studied at the Etz Chaim Yeshiva."}, "D4S3": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0364-395b1e3fa824:d03", "start": 366, "end": 503, "text": "In 1932 he was expelled from Etz Chaim for unseemly conduct at a Purim party, where he allegedly slighted chief rabbi Abraham Isaac Kook."}, "D4S4": {"document_number": 4, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0364-395b1e3fa824:d03", "start": 504, "end": 577, "text": "(He later stated that he did not know ahead of time that Rabbi Kook would"}, "D5S1": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0364-395b1e3fa824:d04", "start": 0, "end": 6, "text": "years."}, "D5S2": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0364-395b1e3fa824:d04", "start": 7, "end": 69, "text": "Some of his children were also leaders of the Yishuv haYashan."}, "D5S3": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0364-395b1e3fa824:d04", "start": 70, "end": 233, "text": "His children were: Rabbi Naftali Zvi Porush (the second), Rabbi Akiva Porush, Rabbi Aaron Porush, Rabbi Eliezer Lipa (Lipman) Porush, Rabbi Liber Mordechai Porush."}, "D5S4": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0364-395b1e3fa824:d04", "start": 234, "end": 308, "text": "A daughter married his brother Gershon's son Rabbi Menachem Mendel Porush."}, "D5S5": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0364-395b1e3fa824:d04", "start": 309, "end": 445, "text": "Another daughter Tzivia married Rabbi Chaim Yehuda Leib Auerbach and their son was Rabbi Shlomo Zalman Auerbach who was named after him."}, "D5S6": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0364-395b1e3fa824:d04", "start": 446, "end": 600, "text": "Shlomo Zalman Porush Rabbi Shlomo Zalman Porush, (), was born in Babruysk, Russian Empire (now Belarus) in 1850 to his father Rabbi Naftali Zvi Porush (d."}, "D5S7": {"document_number": 5, "doc_id": "ramdocs-0364-395b1e3fa824:d04", "start": 601, "end": 626, "text": "1